  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nThe eight A-copy sweeps do not absorb the QQ16 paired shear\u2019s eight extra native lines. At the actual `B_1_2[:80]` cut, before future-Y alignment, the sheared endpoint needs **exactly 24 atomic single-field native lines versus 16 inherited**. A 24-by-24 character-difference minor has determinant **4096**, and a typed owned-C0 word attains the bound.\n\nThe theorem allows arbitrary finite scalar resynthesis with coefficients uniform over owners/payload addresses, plus free orthogonal-owner cover maps with even translations. All 64 actual map events belong to this subgroup. It holds for every positive tensor length. Odd translations, other payload-address operations, multi-field native atoms, internal-wrapper splitting and later cuts are excluded. This is a scoped native-cost result, not a controller, supplier or \u03ba improvement.\n\nThe complete local invoice is **16\u219224 lines, 32\u219248 native wrappers, 64\u219264 explicit maps, 48\u219272 complex ADDs, 16\u219232 CLEARs and 8\u219216 private sweeps**. Scalar real-primitive allowance is **480\u2192704 (+224)**, charging half ADDs at 10, unit ADDs at 8 and CLEARs at 2. Global hosting, precision and recursive admission remain open.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nArtifact head `f2c93e76f84ad4ef14441d97e731cc761db0975c`. Base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, priority revision 4. One chooser seed `f7a0c6caa6b3f1906aa449affcb084ab`; recursive-interfaces / joint-query-controller, key `22e535909f1d243e7553`. [TASK.json](https://github.com/ToikY/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f2c93e76f84ad4ef14441d97e731cc761db0975c/research/qq16-even-map-native-cut/TASK.json) explicitly records **changed** scope: PR #2328\u2019s released later-cut physical-cost handoff replaces the already-covered generic extra-observation experiment. It does not complete the original controller gate.\n\nCanonical [investigation/claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2205#discussioncomment-18944331). The 08:24 UTC refresh paginated 619 open PR bodies including drafts; #2328 remains at `6b2717ce2bbb13c2152e64efea48867b78840bbb`. Main/guidance/catalogue/selected record are unchanged. The canonical thread and targeted board/handoffs were read; broad Discussion/closed/unpublished coverage is incomplete. No first-closure claim.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/qq16-even-map-native-cut\n```\n\nCPython 3.12.14 / macOS arm64: registered normal and optimized replay passes, with **13 semantic controls and nine integration tests in each mode**. Metadata/Git-object pins and whitespace checks pass.\n\nFresh evidence includes 712-row equality in a free noncommuting-operator algebra (all positive tensor lengths by written interpretation), a separate complete **\u03bb=1** affine-group replay, all 480 dirty helpers, C0 cleanup/C1..C7 preservation, ordered native frames/barriers, and 8,192 literal native-recipe basis columns. An independent real rational 48-by-48 check yields rank 48 and determinant 4096\u00b2. Controls distinguish tensor powers from a simultaneous-shift surrogate, detect a helper corruption invisible to both characters, and reject bad native phases, owner routes, scratch ownership, receipts and source bytes. No pending predecessor verifier is imported. Separate agent math and test reviews found no remaining blocker; no human or proof-assistant review.\n\nThe broad research-baseline command was attempted but did not pass because this sparse checkout lacks the selected supplier\u2019s complete source inventory. Full selected/supplier replay, physical compilation, global precision and all-size obligations were not run. This package\u2019s pinned closure and registered replay pass.\n\n## Credit\n\ncommdata2338 (#2328, exact head above): earlier 16-line theorem, character-difference method, typed prefix and later-cut handoff. Charles Bethin / cbethin (#2252, `6dd49c2b186e08ef1f3efd08f62e1add97ff04a3`): native-frame correction. Cinna Davis / 1337isnot1337 (#2216, `b80e9ba43367fb8b20877a97da1cb677c34f9264`): logical paired shear. Ali Romman / aliromman (#1969, `a6e6ad3936f67b8f63b5b68c5e75d540610a65e7`) and retained lineage: maps, recipes, words and notices.\n\nNew work by ToikY with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance and separate agent reviews, Apache-2.0. Existing sources/notices unchanged.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n[README follow-ups](https://github.com/ToikY/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f2c93e76f84ad4ef14441d97e731cc761db0975c/research/qq16-even-map-native-cut/README.md#open-next-questions): specify a later cut or expanded map alphabet before testing fusion; separately screen any sufficient retained record against #2368/#2381 before native costing. No selected frontier change or merge is requested.",
